# xv6 Shared Memory & Custom System Calls

An implementation of shared memory mechanisms and process management system calls inside MIT's **xv6** operating system (an x86 multi-core Unix-like OS written in C).

## 🚀 Implemented Features

- **Shared Memory Subsystem:** Implemented `shm_open` and `shm_close` system calls to allow IPC (Inter-Process Communication) via shared virtual memory pages.
- **Custom System Calls:** Added process monitoring system calls (`getprocinfo`) to trace system resource usage.
- **Kernel Modifications:** Modified page tables (`kalloc.c`, `vm.c`) and process structure (`proc.h`, `proc.c`) to maintain shared memory maps across context switches.

## 🛠 Tech Stack

- **Languages:** C, x86 Assembly
- **Tools & Environment:** QEMU Emulator, GCC, Make, GDB

